From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Belfast Patches <belfast-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:01:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Paint UK road markings on UK roads (centre, lane, warning,
 edge, Stop and Give Way lines)

A level whose road rules are the United Kingdom's (countryCode GB) gets UK paint
from one table, services/ukRoadMarkings.js: material, textureLength and width per
pattern (TSM 3 and 5, TSRGD 2016, TSR (NI) 1997). The materials are named
uk_*_cubewood; their textures are shipped with the level by the Belfast pipeline.

- Lines (buildLineMarkingLayers, restyled): centre 1008 / 1008.1 and lane 1005 /
  1005.1 by speed limit (small module up to 40 mph, large above), edge 1012.1,
  double white 1013.1 from overtaking=no or overtaking:forward|backward=no, and a
  warning line 1004 / 1004.1 over the last 5 to 10 marks where the centre line
  stops at a junction. Widths 100 or 150 mm painted; DecalRoad width = paint / 0.75.
  Left-hand traffic: the centre and lane lines of unequal lane counts are mirrored
  so the forward lanes are on the left, as the AI lanes are.
- Junctions (the stop-bar pass): Stop line 1002.1 at STOP signs, 1001 at signals,
  and a Give Way line 1003A with a triangle 1023A per lane at the give-way
  approaches the sign code already finds. Give-ways at roundabouts are left alone.

Every other country is unchanged (getMarkingStyle and the sign sets are untouched).

